    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "720d6c4c_ad45733c",
        "filename": "board/hammer/battery.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 57,
      "author": {
        "id": 1182824
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-17T17:36:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Most detachable bases do not have a battery. Therefore, I believe that the default value for BP_NO would be more appropriate.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 57,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 57,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "d841dc7a0092f49c8cc574eae2ced31a5d3f2d89",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "df1cf614_13929885",
        "filename": "board/hammer/battery.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 57,
      "author": {
        "id": 1141739
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-18T03:00:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "battery.c depends on `CONFIG_BATTERY_SMART \u003d\u003d 1`. so we can assume that the battery exists.\n\n(Also I think we can assume that both CONFIG_BATTERY_SMART and CONFIG_BATTERY_PRESENT_GPIO are enabled, no need to support other combinations)",
      "parentUuid": "720d6c4c_ad45733c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 57,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 57,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "d841dc7a0092f49c8cc574eae2ced31a5d3f2d89",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c70ee04b_54d16a63",
        "filename": "board/hammer/battery.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 57,
      "author": {
        "id": 1524179
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-18T03:22:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Only the \"wand\" has the battery, and only its config in variant.h specifies the config `CONFIG_BATTERY_SMART`, then \"battery.c\" is included for compiling. As a result, I think if the base is not sensing the battery via `CONFIG_BATTERY_PRESENT_GPIO`, probably we will always assume the battery is present.\n\nJust a heads-up, as using `battery_is_present` for fixing b/290553696 may not be a suitable approach, probably I will abandon these CL in the future.",
      "parentUuid": "df1cf614_13929885",
